  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    Frost-ward Silvmococriaa~ Tier is a Weal' Clique~ operative — one of the Nightshelf faction charged with bitter stewardship of the Glow-Fissure, the corruption breach-point that bleeds taint into both civilizations. She carries a fire-core pouch at her throat and touches it when consulting Mandatum∴absconditu, the Nightshelf doctrine that survival demands secrecy. The gesture marks the boundary between what she is permitted to say and what needs saying.
    
    Silvmococriaa~ can map corruption's shape by temperature alone, a skill earned through sustained proximity to the Glow-Fissure's taint. This was knowledge she never intended to share with surface-dwellers.
    
    At Dawn Naong, a crystal-vaulted trade hub where corruption had fouled the ice-memory, she worked alongside Fimalin, an Aurora-trained ice reader, and her Nightshelf colleague ☽'mortoth. When ☽'mortoth initially refused full collaboration, Silvmococriaa~ returned alone to provide the fire-core thermal mapping that enabled a hybrid technique — placing fire-cores against corrupted ice to define thermal boundaries that aurora-light could follow beneath the tainted layer. Over nine hours across two days, the method recovered seven memory-layers and produced an eastern shallows krill-bloom prediction that proved accurate eleven days later.
    
    The technique exists only partially documented across two separate traditions. The cost of Silvmococriaa~'s decision to share it was negotiated in coded cant and never explained to Fimalin.
    
    She flinches at the sound ice makes when a memory-layer cracks open wrong. She does not explain this either.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771735762241_0", anchor: "The technique exists only partially documented across two separate traditions.", text: "A survival tool — demonstrated, functional, proven accurate within eleven days — deliberately fragmented across two knowledge systems because doctrine requires it. Mandatum∴absconditu says survival demands secrecy. Way∴ens says fire-core knowledge must flow freely. Both claim to serve survival. When Dawn Naong's corruption returns, and it will — the Glow-Fissure has never stopped bleeding — someone will need to reinvent this hybrid method from nothing, because the Nightshelf half is locked in coded cant and the Aurora half lacks the thermal framework to make sense of itself. This is the Flipper Accord's deepest pathology: two civilizations that cannot survive apart, maintaining ignorance of each other's methods as a point of identity.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771735762241_1", anchor: "She flinches at the sound ice makes when a memory-layer cracks open wrong.", text: "Wrong-cracking has a specific acoustic signature — a pitch that drops when it should rise, as if the memory resists release. You do not forget it once you have heard it. You certainly do not need it explained.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
